<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=pottery">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Tools and materials</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pottery</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pottery is the craft and products of forming vessels and other objects from clay fired at high temperatures; the earliest known pottery vessels, from Xianren Cave in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangxi">Jiangxi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, date to 20,000–19,000 years ago. Ceramic figurines are older: the Venus of Dolní Věstonice in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a> is dated to 29,000–25,000 BCE. Pottery appears to have been developed independently in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sub-saharan-africa">sub-Saharan Africa</a>, where finds in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a> date to at least 9,400 BCE, and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>. Durable pottery sherds are typically the most common artefacts to survive on archaeological sites.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pottery.jpg" alt="Pottery" width="320" height="348" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Altamura Painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Altamura_Painter_-_Red-Figure_Calyx_Krater_-_Walters_48262_-_Side_A.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>c. 18,000 BCE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Xianren Cave, Jiangxi, China</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Also arose independently</span>Ounjougou, Mali (by 9400 BCE); Brazil (9,500–5,000 years ago)</p><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Fired-clay figurines are older: those of Dolní Věstonice in the Czech Republic date to 29,000–25,000 BCE.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/control-of-fire">Control of fire<span>c. 1 million years ago</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/potters-wheel">Potter's wheel<span>c. 4500 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/glassmaking">Glassmaking<span>c. 2500 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/porcelain">Porcelain<span>25–220 CE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=pottery">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
